\tag{fdip}
\title{Group-algebra sectors}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{The half-turn acts through a [group algebra](fdip-000L).
When two is invertible, its projectors separate algebraic sectors.
The real Gaussian law admits the corresponding [orthogonal calculation](fdip-000M),
while [characteristic two](fdip-000N) tests the exact boundary of that
decomposition.}

\transclude{fdip-000L}
\transclude{fdip-000M}
\transclude{fdip-000N}
